      "widgets_values": [
        "For the target video, at 0.00 seconds into the target video, <Picture 1> (from [Shot 1]) is fully referenced.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action, photorealistic smartphone mirror-selfie video with natural indoor daylight, realistic skin microtexture, physically believable fabric response, subtle smartphone sensor texture, and restrained cinematic contrast. The adult woman shown in <Picture 1> remains in the same crouching pose, preserving her identity, facial structure, body proportions, green fantasy outfit, phone, cardboard sign, mirror composition, room, plants, lighting direction, and visible background objects. The camera holds a static shot with imperceptible natural handheld micro-movement only. Her right hand continuously maintains the same grip and position around the phone, and her left hand continuously maintains the same grip and position around the cardboard sign.\n\nFrom 0.00 to 0.55 seconds, she looks at the phone screen, takes a subtle breath, and prepares to speak. From 0.55 to 5.85 seconds, the confident woman with a natural conversational voice (S1) speaks directly to the phone with restrained, realistic lip, jaw, cheek, and facial movement: <d>[English] Want to make videos like this? Fire AI teaches open-source photo and video creation, completely free.</d> She makes one natural blink and one very small head adjustment while both hands, the phone, and the sign remain stable. From 5.85 seconds to the end, she closes her mouth naturally and gives a small confident smile while maintaining the same pose and framing. The handwritten text already visible on the cardboard sign remains unchanged and readable. Mirror geometry, reflection alignment, anatomy, lighting, facial identity, and background object positions remain temporally consistent throughout the continuous shot.\n\noverall_soundscape: Clean close-recorded female speech over quiet indoor room tone, with subtle breathing and extremely faint clothing movement. No echo, additional voices, or artificial sound effects.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A",
        1344,
        768,
        158
      ]
